{"type":"assistant.message","data":{"messageId":"c0c75de7-f579-423d-8a88-5380344bd30d","content":"Edit [`renderers/tinymce/src/icon-pack.ts`](renderers/tinymce/src/icon-pack.ts), specifically `ICON_ALIASES`:\n\n```ts\nconst ICON_ALIASES: Record<string, string> = {\n  bold: \"text\",\n  close: \"circle-x\",\n  \"action-next\": \"chevron-right\",\n};\n```\n\nThe left side is the TinyMCE icon name; the right side is the Pantoken/Lucide token name.\n\nOne subtlety: direct token names take priority over aliases:\n\n```ts\nconst pantokenName = pantokenIcons.has(tinymceIconName)\n  ? tinymceIconName\n  : ICON_ALIASES[tinymceIconName];\n```\n\nSo aliases only affect names without an existing matching token. To remap an existing icon such as `bold`, change this resolver to prefer aliases:\n\n```ts\nconst pantokenName = ICON_ALIASES[tinymceIconName] ?? tinymceIconName;\n```\n\nThen run:\n\n```sh\nvp test renderers/tinymce/tests/icon-pack.test.ts\n```","toolRequests":[],"reasoningText":""},"id":"239a732c-8b60-4bf1-b993-e16febeababb","timestamp":"2026-09-22T22:39:24.896Z","parentId":"8a6ca5bc-8077-4268-aeb3-064651ec35b2"}
